{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe nurse reviews a commercial driver's symptoms alongside information from a witness, the treating team and an older workplace form, because each source describes a different part of the story; the occupational record retains those differences and identifies completed current findings without turning a booking, a family account or a recollection into a measured patient result.\n\nThe completed audiogram identifies unaided better-ear average hearing loss of 48 dB across 0.5, 1, 2 and 3 kHz, and the current clinical assessment records possible hearing loss; a hearing aid has been ordered rather than functionally assessed, the audiologist's advice about aided performance is not yet available, and the driver's belief that amplification will solve the difficulty is retained as an expectation rather than evidence that an aided standard has already been met.\n\nThe driver alternates urban deliveries with a longer motorway leg and describes a busy depot where engine noise, glare and interrupted meals can complicate an account of symptoms; the nurse records the work setting as context, while keeping the dated clinical findings distinct from the driver's explanation for why a symptom might have occurred on that shift.\n\nThe nurse reads the summary back to the driver to check the chronology and separates agreement about the wording from verification of a medical finding, then attaches the identified clinical material; any decision about further investigation or work allocation remains for the reviewing professional, and the note itself does not certify that all relevant clinical questions have been answered.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
